#   1204:   5429: ! [file:line.char,errcnt] "error message"
#   1204:   5430: ! 
#   1204:   5431: ! The first two lines are the line being parsed, and an up arrow to the current
#   1204:   5432: ! character position. This part of the display can be removed or inserted by
#   1204:   5433: ! the pl (print line) flag.
#   1204:   5434: ! 
#   1204:   5435: ! The last line, which allways appears, is the filename, line number and
#   1204:   5436: ! character position that is current. If the current line comes from a buffer,
#   1204:   5437: ! the filename and line will not appear. The reasons for not printing this
#   1204:   5438: ! information include personal taste, and the fact that the line may have already
#   1204:   5439: ! been printed, perhaps as a source listing or command line entry.
#   1204:   5440: ! 
#   1204:   5441: ! Note that no line return preceeds the sequence. The caller is responsible for
